            "review_title": "Review at Ty Ai - Bun Cha Ca Quy Nhon",
            "review_text": "brendanhoranhk\nHong Kong, China143 contributions\n0\nSmall local noodle shop , quite good.\nJan 2016 • Couples\nWalked past this place while looking for another restaurant. \nIt looked good, had lots of locals eating and getting take away. \n\nNo chance of English menus or anyone speaking English. \nHowever the staff where very friendly towards us. \n\nEnded up with a noodle soup unsure what meat was in this but I think it may of been tongue or some other offal. (Not quite sure to be honest) \nNoodles where round vs the flat white noodles I have seen elsewhere\nCame with a side of herbs , bean sprouts and chilli. \n\nWe also got some rice paper rolls. \nThey where bigger than expected but tasted amazing. \nStuffed with herbs, vedgi meat and something else that was crunchy. (not sure what) \nServed with a spicy but fruity dip. \nBest rice paper rolls I have had yet. (Not that I have had a lot) \n\nPrice was good. I would go back it was one of the better noodle's I had in Ho Chi Minh City.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 16, 2016",
